  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nA low pressure system continues to sit over the New England \narea which favors dry conditions with seasonable temperatures \nfor our region. A slight rise in temperatures will be seen as \nthe ridge moving in from the West and the heights aloft rise \nthrough the end of the week. \n\nA trough will be moving through the region going into the weekend. \nIncreasing cloud cover will be seen due to the trough-induced lift \nand moisture. This will also allow for showers across the \nregion Saturday night into Sunday morning. 90-95 percent of the\nensemble models show that there is no concern for flash flood \nrisk, while few models do show a slight chance for low-end flood\nrisks to occur. This concern is pending on the track and depth \nof the trough as it moves into the Northeast.",
